# Pairs with ListedRestorable. Production before the fix of #5412: a pass
# read its catalog listing BEFORE it checked the one-pass guard, so it could
# wait out another pass and then plan from a listing that still held rows
# that pass had pruned since. Its scan could then find an increment built on
# one of them and restore the row of a backup whose manifest and artifact were
# already gone. The mutant plans from every row ever registered (pub), which
# over-approximates any listing taken before the guard; the same interleaving
# was confirmed against a model that splits the listing from the guard, as
# production ordered them (see #5412).
MODULE: ListedRestorableListingBeforeGuard
TARGET: ListedRestorable
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a pass plans from a catalog listing taken before its one-pass guard
PERTURBS: PruneList

--- FIND
    \* The listing, read under the guard.
    /\ LET L == cat
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: the listing was read before the guard, and may still hold
    \* rows another pass has pruned since.
    /\ LET L == pub
--- END
